# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# rust/anchor
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock

# Redis writes its snapshot into whatever directory it was started from, which
# while running this project's tests is the repository root. It is a database
# file, and one that has held session tokens and single-use quote locks — not
# something to keep in version control even when the values are from a
# throwaway instance.
dump.rdb
*.rdb
